  #line-at(90.024pt, 231.17pt, "ABSTRACT: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(167.42pt, 231.17pt, "Uncertainty quantification in thermoreflectance measurements of ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 247.49pt, "multilayer structures is challenging because thermophysical-property extraction ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 263.81pt, "involves nonlinear inverse problems with strongly coupled parameters. Covariance-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 280.13pt, "based analytical propagation is efficient but assumes local linearity and approximately ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 296.45pt, "Gaussian fitted variables, whereas Monte Carlo (MC) propagation captures non-")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 312.77pt, "Gaussian behavior but is computationally expensive and can be unreliable when ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 328.97pt, "simultaneously fitting parameters spanning very different orders of magnitude. Here, ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 345.29pt, "we address these issues by combining normalized MC sampling, used to obtain reliable ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 361.61pt, "benchmark distributions, with physics-based variable transformations for analytical ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 377.93pt, "uncertainty propagation. From the multilayer heat-diffusion equation, we identify ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 394.39pt, "natural coordinates: the interfacial thermal resistance ")
