  #line-at(72.024pt, 291.05pt, "S1. Numerical effect of fitting-variable normalization ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(96.024pt, 311.69pt, "Each Monte Carlo (MC) realization for the Al–GaN–AlGaN–Si case was fitted twice, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 332.45pt, "once using the original dimensional parameters and once using the normalized parameters. The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 353.09pt, "two fits used identical realizations of the known input parameters, identical signal perturbations, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 373.85pt, "and identical physical parameter bounds. Figure S1 compares the final objective-function ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 394.49pt, "values obtained from the two parameterizations on a trial-by-trial basis. Normalized fitting ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 415.25pt, "yields a lower final objective-function value in every trial, while the corresponding root-mean-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 435.91pt, "square fitting residuals remain comparable to the experimental noise level. These results ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 456.67pt, "confirm that the discrepancy between the two MC distributions arises from numerical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 477.31pt, "convergence effects associated with poor parameter scaling. ")
